# AermadeMarkdown

Convert office documents, PDFs, and HTML files to Markdown. Designed for bulk conversion of project libraries into AI-ready markdown files.

## Supported formats

| Extension | Converter |
|-----------|-----------|
| `.docx` | MarkItDown |
| `.html`, `.htm` | MarkItDown |
| `.pptx` | MarkItDown |
| `.xlsx`, `.xlsm`, `.xls` | MarkItDown |
| `.pdf` | PyMuPDF4LLM (long text-only) or MarkItDown (short/image-heavy) |

The PDF converter automatically selects the best backend based on page count and image density.

## Setup

```bash
python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -e .
```

## Usage

```bash
# Convert all files in ./input to ./output
md-convert

# Convert a single file
md-convert path/to/file.pdf

# Convert a folder to a specific output directory
md-convert path/to/folder -o path/to/output

# Inject YAML frontmatter into each output file
md-convert --frontmatter

# Raise errors instead of writing failure placeholders
md-convert --strict
```

## Output

Each converted file is written as `.md`, mirroring the input folder structure. Alongside the output, a `conversion_manifest.jsonl` log is written with the status, converter used, warnings, and errors for each file. Files that fail produce an empty `_failed_to_convert.md` placeholder unless `--strict` is passed.

## Frontmatter

Pass `--frontmatter` to prepend YAML metadata to each output file:

```yaml
---
converted_at: '2026-06-29T05:33:16+00:00'
converter: html_converter
source: report.html
source_path: C:\path\to\report.html
source_type: .html
title: Q3 Cost Report
---
```

Fields: `source`, `source_path`, `source_type`, `converter`, `converted_at`. `title` is included when extractable from the source. `warnings` is included if the conversion produced any.

## Adding a converter

1. Create a class inheriting from `BaseConverter` in `src/md_converter/converters/`.
2. Set `supported_extensions` and `name`.
3. Implement `convert(self, input_path: Path) -> ConversionResult`.
4. Add an instance to `ConverterRegistry` in `src/md_converter/core/registry.py`.
